    "note": "TCWind_JTWC._gtcmProfile's continuity factor for eq. (3) is A = (ri/rm)**x1 * (rm/ri)**x2. Matching the two branches at r = ri requires the reciprocal, A = (rm/ri)**x1 * (ri/rm)**x2; as written the outer branch is scaled by (ri/rm)**(2*(x1-x2)) and the modelled wind STEPS at ri. riStep measures that step in the field as built. gtcmWithContinuousRi is the whole coherence block recomputed with the continuity-preserving factor patched in at runtime (the fit is redone too), so a reader can separate what the GTCM model does from what this one line does. Nothing is fixed here: GFE/procedures/TCWind_JTWC.py is the reference implementation and this verification does not own it. The step is reported to the maintainer, not worked around.",
